**If we go by your premise, the answer is 90 days. But that isn't what Nevada law actually says.**

I won't use the deposit-law tools, as you asked, so this is from my own general knowledge rather than a reviewed guide. As far as I know, **Nevada landlords have 30 days** after the tenancy ends to return the deposit, under NRS 118A.242. They must return it along with an itemized list of any deductions. If a landlord withholds the deposit in bad faith, the tenant may be able to recover up to double the deposit amount.

If you're asking about a proposed change, a hypothetical or a lease term, I'm happy to work with the 90-day number. If you're dealing with a real deposit, plan around 30 days unless you've confirmed the law changed. Check the current statute or ask a local tenant resource or attorney. This is general information, not legal advice.